  "description": "Pure C# JPEG XL plugin for PictureSharp. Detects and identifies JPEG XL files (raw codestream and container), decodes still lossy (VarDCT, XYB) and lossless (Modular) images, including recompressed JPEGs, patches and progressive files, encodes images lossily (VarDCT with quality, distance and effort 1-9, about as small as cjxl, the default) or losslessly (8-bit or 16-bit Modular, about as small as cjxl -d 0 -e 7), losslessly transcodes sequential and progressive 8-bit JPEG with byte-exact original reconstruction, and reads, writes and edits the ICC profile, EXIF and XMP (also Brotli-compressed).",
  "id": "PictureSharp.Jxl",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-30T10:31:17.45Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "eSM4waN262RHsjAhwyiifchuHfUxEz+BA1F5Eu91xv/ObbXo4NCyBKknZa/qDyt5TXc5SbBUPXGumlxAILnk4A==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 353754,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/art-ix/picturesharp.jxl",
  "published": "2026-10-30T10:21:32.64Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.8.6: less memory for large images, with identical output: JPEG-recompressed 4:2:0 images are upsampled and converted per row band while writing pixels, lossless encoding transforms group copies and records predictor errors in its token storage, lossy encoding releases its working image early, Modular decoding and JPEG reconstruction no longer allocate per block. Per 12 MP image: JPEG decode peak 332 to 180 MiB (1.9x faster with 16 threads), lossless encode 1192 to 864 MiB and 976 to 576 MB allocated, 16-bit lossless decode allocates half as much. No API changes. See docs/releases/release-0.8.6.md and docs/benchmarks/speed.md.",
